# handle-hover-move (h7-plane, re-pinned by ea29aa9 at c6754e7): the pointer
# from the diamond straight onto the square in ONE move. The hover-end and the
# new hover fire in the same move, but hovering is now the hovered index
# (ea29aa9): grab-hover. A stepped move would re-hover; the single jump is the
# state.
#
# Re-pinned again at c6754e7 (7686c89): under this query P sits at plane
# (2, -1) — the square's own place — so the marker beats the coincident handle
# (the hit test's last-index rule) and P, which has no onHover handler, wins the
# hover. The lit line is therefore EMPTY, not "a and b lit": read on ref-h11 at
# c6754e7, WebKit/Chromium/Firefox alike, the cursor is grab-hover and nothing
# is lit (the same query with p=5, P away from the square, lights a and b).
# The spec expected a and b lit; the reference reads nothing lit.
# Behaviour: cursor grab-hover; the lit line empty.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
query func=x2&a=2&h=1&k=-3
wait 500
move 978 640
wait 300
move 1028 540
wait 300
shot handle-hover-move
